    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nThree changes, following the existing `locality` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a derivation helper mirroring `Locality`: `Timezone.of(owner)` maps the owner's region (from `Locality.of(owner)`) through the fixed region-to-timezone table, returning `null` when the region is unknown/unmapped.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` wiring `timezone` to `Timezone.of(owner)`, exactly alongside the existing `locality` mapping.\n\nThe acceptance test (`knownOwner(\"Sydney\")` \u2192 postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, as does the rest of the suite.",
